[[Open This|Helios Remote Host Changed]]

---

```yml
michael@DESKTOP-J7AHM1I:~/helios-engvm$ ssh michael@192.168.1.23
@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@
@    WARNING: REMOTE HOST IDENTIFICATION HAS CHANGED!     @
@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@
IT IS POSSIBLE THAT SOMEONE IS DOING SOMETHING NASTY!
Someone could be eavesdropping on you right now (man-in-the-middle attack)!
It is also possible that a host key has just been changed.
The fingerprint for the ED25519 key sent by the remote host is
SHA256:f+OwUBYq7tP9pvcRBc1JclUYRb7uGE5NpLZXZrgGZ3I.
Please contact your system administrator.
Add correct host key in /home/michael/.ssh/known_hosts to get rid of this message.
Offending ED25519 key in /home/michael/.ssh/known_hosts:9
  remove with:
  ssh-keygen -f '/home/michael/.ssh/known_hosts' -R '192.168.1.23'
Host key for 192.168.1.23 has changed and you have requested strict checking.
Host key verification failed.
```

In the same terminal where you’re trying to SSH, run:

```
ssh-keygen -f '/home/michael/.ssh/known_hosts' -R '192.168.1.23'
```

```
ssh-keygen -f "$env:USERPROFILE\.ssh\known_hosts" -R "192.168.1.23"
```

Then try SSH again:

```
ssh michael@192.168.1.23
```